@AAGresearch You can note how I simply excluded First Majestics lead (PB). 

That imo is the real problem when companies try to sell especially lead as "silver equivalent". Imo only gold should be included in that and it probably should be at least 40% silver (60% gold) in that number.

Further I increasingly prefer silver producers that produce dore bar rather than a concentrate that has to be refined in China. This due to rapidly changing geopolitics.

@deruyter1667 In general the buying company sees a falling share price. In this case AG would go to 45m ounces of silver production and the mine quality would improve as VZLA has a better asset. 

I think AG would quickly revert to a higher valuation than before due to improved quality and larger size.

But I only used AG as One example of the many companies that very likely would want VZLA. Partly due to both AG and VZLA having Mexican assets making the MCAP comparison even more useful.

@ineedjonathan I fact checked your GROK statement: 
" particularly in 2003, 2018, 2019, 2022, and 2025, have led to more significant disruptions."

So I would say your statement is not correct.

@ineedjonathan It is not at all rare to see Swedish reactors offline and causing a lot higher electricity prices.

I have seen it many times. Right now, half of them I think the article said.

France I have historically have this problem with heat in the summer and the cooling water many years.

@OilTanker_GenX @MikeHor43947875 I think it is a smart way of investing, to identify capable people with integrity. Some are likely to drop of from the list while others will be added depending how they act and manage the various difficulties that come a long.

Another interesting person to follow is Alex Langer at $SM.v Sierra Madre. Hard working, many years left in the business and increasingly backed by very competent investors (as shown in the latest placement).

Already producing Silver/Gold in a property I have known about for over 10years and share Alex opinion that this is a district that is likely to grow.

@OilTanker_GenX @MikeHor43947875 I am a long term thinker and planner. I am thinking that some time in 2026 I will reach a point when any additional $ portfolio value earned should be moved to shipping.

I would then expect that to continue during 2027 and maybe even 2028 making me look stupid as PM continues to outperform.

Nobody objective can accuse me of being conservative. But, being somewhat more of that is what this thinking is all about. We should have years of mining bull market, but the more we celebrate that the more valuable it is to have some kind of automatic ongoing diversification system in place.

